    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/05/saucony-endorphin-speed-5-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length PWRRUN PB feels softer than v4 with good heel and forefoot protection, a smoother heel transition, and forefoot cushioning that no longer bottoms out on long runs.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is bouncy and responsive with moderate nylon-plate snappiness up front, but it is slightly less aggressive/fast than v4 or top super shoes.",
        "Stability: Though neutral, it has mild guidance from plate geometry (medial guidance/lateral bias), some torsional rigidity, a stiff heel counter, and generally secure lateral support with only mild midfoot slip on turns.",
        "Durability: Traction is fair with strategic XT-900 rubber, but exposed PWRRUN PB shows early wear (noted around 45 miles, including posterolateral heel), indicating average overall longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/05/saucony-endorphin-speed-5-multi-tester.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: PWRRUN PB is notably firm rather than plush (36/28 mm stack), giving controlled impact protection with a heel/forefoot feel geared more to smooth rolling than softness.",
        "Responsiveness: The shoe is quick, snappy, and efficient (SPEEDROLL + nylon plate), but bounce and perceived energy return are moderate rather than highly springy.",
        "Stability: A key strength, with plate-driven torsional rigidity, a more secure higher heel counter, strong heel hold, and added medial-side support for confident lateral control/cornering.",
        "Durability: Improved via added strategic outsole rubber and coverage; traction is excellent and testers saw minimal outsole wear after roughly 40 miles."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/saucony-endorphin-speed-5-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The PWRRUN PB midsole gives a balanced soft feel with good impact protection (36 mm heel / 28 mm forefoot), but it is not especially plush for easy-run comfort.",
        "Responsiveness: Ride quality is lively and bouncy with strong energy return for tempo work, though it is less snappy than more aggressive carbon-plated options.",
        "Stability: Fit feels secure around the heel/collar, but the plate redesign (single medial wing) increases torsional and forefoot flexibility, trading some rigid lateral support for smoother movement.",
        "Durability: The shoe held up well on unexpected dirt-road/light-trail use with no major breakdown noted, but the upper showed cosmetic dirt quickly and long-term outsole wear data was limited."
      ]
    }
